{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Deceive_Reality","to":"Deceive Reality"},{"from":"Masterful_Stab","to":"Masterful Stab"},{"from":"Endless_Agony","to":"Endless Agony"},{"from":"Dramatic_Entrance","to":"Dramatic Entrance"},{"from":"Feel_No_Pain","to":"Feel No Pain"},{"from":"Defend_(Watcher)","to":"Defend (Watcher)"},{"from":"Dagger_Throw","to":"Dagger Throw"}],"pages":{"2026":{"pageid":2026,"ns":0,"title":"Backstab","revisions":[{"revid":56888,"parentid":55632,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Backstab\n| Image       = Green-Backstab.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = {{KW|Innate}}.<br>Deal (11;15) damage.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Innate, Exhaust\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Innate}}\n{{C|Backstab}} is a 0 {{Icon|GE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 11 (15 if upgraded) damage. {{C|Backstab}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself. It has {{KW|Innate}}, meaning it will always be in the first hand of combat.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Wrist Blade}} increases the damage of this card by 4.\n\n* As this {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card is {{KW|Innate}}, it guarantees that it will be able to benefit from the {{BD|Vulnerable}} applied by {{R|Bag of Marbles}} and the temporary {{BD|Strength}} gained from {{R|Mutagenic Strength}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The Beta Art for this card depicts a Caesar salad, because Julius Caesar is a historical figure who was famously betrayed and stabbed to death by his senators on the Ides of March.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Update 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Backstab buffed: Cost lowered to 0. Damage decreased to 11.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2459":{"pageid":2459,"ns":0,"title":"Beta","revisions":[{"revid":53190,"parentid":50755,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"#REDIRECT [[Alpha#Beta]]"}}}]},"2322":{"pageid":2322,"ns":0,"title":"Burn","revisions":[{"revid":56921,"parentid":55674,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Burn\n|Image       = Colorless-Burn.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Status\n|Rarity      = Status\n|Cost        = -2\n|Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.<br>At the end of your turn, take (2;4) damage.\n|GivesToPlayer = Unplayable\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}}\n{{C|Burn}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|Common:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} Card. Burn is the ONLY status card that can be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}}.\n\n== Obtaining Burn ==\nPlaying {{C|Immolate}} or {{C|Overclock}} will add a Burn to the player's discard pile.\n\nThe following enemies can give the player Burns:\n* {{M|Hexaghost}}\n** {{Int|Hexaghost|Sear}} - Adds 1({{Asc|19|2}}) {{C|Burn|Burns}} into your discard pile.\n** {{Int|Hexaghost|Inferno}} - Adds 3 {{C|Burn|Burns+}} into your discard pile. Upgrades all {{C|Burn|Burns}}. For the rest of combat, any {{C|Burn|Burns}} created by {{Int|Hexaghost|Sear}} will be upgraded.\n* {{M|Orb Walker}}\n** {{Int|Orb Walker|Laser}} - Adds a {{C|Burn}} into your draw pile, and another {{C|Burn}} into your discard pile.\n* {{M|Nemesis}}\n** {{Int|Nemesis|Tri Burn}} - Adds 3({{Asc|18|5}}) {{C|Burn|Burns}} into your discard pile.\n* {{M|Spire Spear}}\n** {{Int|Spire Spear|Burn Strike}} - Adds 2 {{C|Burn|Burns}} into your discard pile({{Asc|18|on top of your draw pile}}).\n* {{M|Corrupt Heart}}\n** {{Int|Corrupt Heart|Debilitate}} - Adds 1 {{C|Burn}} into your draw pile.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n\n* If the player loses health due to unblocked damage from Burn while {{C|Rupture}} is in play, the damage from Burn will trigger Rupture's {{BD|Strength}} gain.\n* If the player loses health due to unblocked damage from Burn while possessing {{R|Self-Forming Clay}}, the damage from Burn will trigger Self-Forming Clay's {{KW|Block}} gain next turn.\n* Triggers the damage from {{C|Fire Breathing}}.\n* Draws cards with {{C|Evolve}}.\n* Is {{KW|Exhaust|exhausted}} by {{C|Second Wind}} and triggers its {{KW|Block}} gain.\n* Can be {{KW|Exhaust|exhausted}} with {{R|Medical Kit}} to trigger exhaust synergies such as {{C|Feel No Pain}} or {{R|Charon's Ashes}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n\n* Burn will contribute 1 {{KW|Block}} gained for {{R|Cloak Clasp}} as the relic triggers before Burn is discarded. This is overall a block penalty due to Burn's damage.\n* Burn's unblocked damage will be reduced by {{R|Tungsten Rod}}.\n* Burn will still be discarded after dealing damage at the end of the turn if the player has {{R|Runic Pyramid}} or {{KW|Retain|retains}} it using {{C|Equilibrium}}, {{C|Well-Laid Plans}}, or {{C|Meditate}}.\n* Is {{KW|Exhaust|exhausted}} by {{C|Sever Soul}} since it's not an {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|Attack}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n\n* If the player loses health due to unblocked damage from {{C|Burn}} while possessing {{R|Centennial Puzzle}} or {{R|Runic Cube}}, the drawn card(s) will be discarded with the rest of their hand.\n* Prevents {{C|Clash}} from being played.\n\n== Trivia ==\n\n* Burn is the only {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} card that has an upgraded version.\n** The only way to obtain a {{C|Burn}}+ is from the {{M|Hexaghost}} converting all Burns in the player's hand, draw pile, and discard pile with Burn+ following their ''Inferno'' attack. Additionally, after the first time ''Inferno'' is used, all of Hexaghost's attacks that would normally give the player a Burn will give the player a Burn+ instead.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Burn cards no longer trigger Time Eater's ability at end of turn.\n** Rebound card no longer puts Burns on top of your deck.\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Fixed issue where Regret/Decay/Doubt/Burn fails to exhaust via Blue Candle and Medical Kit.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n{{DefectNav}}\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1788":{"pageid":1788,"ns":0,"title":"Dagger Throw","revisions":[{"revid":56359,"parentid":55409,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Dagger Throw\n| Image       = Green-DaggerThrow.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Deal (9;12) damage.<br>Draw 1 card. <br>Discard 1 card.\n| GivesToPlayer = Draw, Discard\n}}\n{{C|Dagger Throw}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 9 (11 if upgraded) damage. It draws 1 card and then makes you select 1 card in your hand to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Selecting a card to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] happens ''after'' drawing, meaning that you can also choose the newly drawn card to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]]. This also means that if you play {{C|Dagger Throw}} without any other cards in hand, it will draw one card and then immediately [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] that card.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Dagger Throw}}'s [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] effect synergises with several [[Silent]] cards and relics: \n\n==== Cards ====\n* [[Keywords#Discard|Discarding]] {{C|Tactician}} or {{C|Reflex}} will immediately activate their effects.\n* {{C|Eviscerate}} is discounted by 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' this turn.\n* {{C|Sneaky Strike}} will now refund 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if also played this turn.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Tough Bandages}} will grant 3 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{R|Tingsha}} will deal 3 damage to a random enemy.\n* {{R|Hovering Kite}} will generate 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if this is the first time a card has been [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] this turn.\n\n=== Neutral === \n* {{C|Dagger Throw}} can also be used to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] cards with end-of-turn effects, like {{C|Burn}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} such as {{C|Regret}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Fixed rare crash with Dagger Throw.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2031":{"pageid":2031,"ns":0,"title":"Dash","revisions":[{"revid":56959,"parentid":55728,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Dash\n|Image       = Green-Dash.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Gain (10;13) {{KW|Block}}.<br>Deal (10;13) damage.\n|GivesToPlayer = Block\n}}\n{{C|Dash}} is a 2 {{Icon|GE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It gives 10 (13 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}, and deals 10 (13 if upgraded) damage.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* The {{KW|Block}} is gained before the damage is dealt or the card is resolved, meaning the {{KW|Block}} already protects from any damage sustained as a result of playing this card through effects like:\n** {{BD|Sharp Hide}} or {{BD|Thorns}}.\n** {{BD|Beat of Death}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Both values are affected separately by effects that change the amount of damage and {{KW|Block}}, such as {{BD|Strength}} and {{BD|Dexterity}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Card Dash+ gets +1 damage and +1 Block.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2425":{"pageid":2425,"ns":0,"title":"Deceive Reality","revisions":[{"revid":56962,"parentid":53296,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Deceive Reality\n|Image       = Purple-DeceiveReality.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (4;7) {{KW|Block}}. <br>Add a {{C|Safety}} into your hand.\n|GivesToPlayer = Block\n}}\n{{C|Deceive Reality}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 4 (7 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}, and adds a {{C|Safety}} into your hand\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* If you have played {{C|Master Reality}} before playing this card, it will add an upgraded {{C|Safety}} to your hand instead.\n\n{{Clear}}\n\n== Safety ==\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Safety\n|Image       = Colorless-Safety.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Special\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = {{KW|Retain}}. <br>Gain (12;16) {{KW|Block}}. <br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Retain, Block, Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Retain}} {{Keyword Infobox|Block}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Safety}} is a 1 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 12 (16 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} and then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}. It has {{KW|Retain}}, meaning it will not be discarded when you end your turn.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1492":{"pageid":1492,"ns":0,"title":"Defend (Watcher)","revisions":[{"revid":56344,"parentid":50630,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Defend (Watcher)\n| DisplayName = Defend\n| Image       = Purple-Defend.png\n| Color       = Purple\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Basic\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Gain (5;8) {{KW|Block}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Defend (Watcher)|Defend}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 5 (8 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}.\n\nThis page is for the Watcher's version of Defend, go here for {{C|Defend (Ironclad)}}, {{C|Defend (Silent)}}, {{C|Defend (Defect)}}.\n\n== Obtaining Defend ==\nThe [[Watcher]] starts with 4 copies of {{C|Defend (Watcher)|Defend}} in her deck. It cannot be obtained through regular card rewards.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2444":{"pageid":2444,"ns":0,"title":"Dramatic Entrance","revisions":[{"revid":55749,"parentid":50723,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Dramatic Entrance\n|Image       = Colorless-DramaticEntrance.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = {{KW|Innate}}.<br>Deal (8;12) damage to ALL enemies.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Innate}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Dramatic Entrance}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 8 (12 if upgraded) damage to '''ALL''' enemies, then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}. It has {{KW|Innate}}, meaning it will always be in the first hand of combat.\n\n== Obtaining Dramatic Entrance ==\n{{C|Dramatic Entrance}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* As this {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card is {{KW|Innate}}, it guarantees that it will be able to benefit from the {{BD|Vulnerable}} applied by {{R|Bag of Marbles}} and the temporary {{BD|Strength}} gained from {{R|Mutagenic Strength}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Dramatic Entrance card buffed. Damage increased from 6 -> 8.\n** Dramatic Entrance+ card buffed. Damage increased from 8 -> 12.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** DramaticEntrance+. Damage 6 -> 8.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2047":{"pageid":2047,"ns":0,"title":"Endless Agony","revisions":[{"revid":55758,"parentid":50504,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Endless Agony\n|Image       = Green-EndlessAgony.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Whenever you draw this card, add a copy of it into your hand.<br>Deal (4;6) damage.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Draw, Hand\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Endless Agony}} is a 0 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 4 (6 if upgraded) damage. {{C|Endless Agony}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself. Whenever this card is drawn, add a copy of it into your hand.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Whenever {{C|Endless Agony}} is drawn, the copy will have the {{Icon|GE}}-cost that the original had ''before'' being drawn. \n** This means that, when drawn with {{BD|Confused}} or {{P|Snecko Oil}}, the original will have its cost randomized ''after'' being copied, meaning that the second copy will still have the cost that the original displayed while it was in the draw pile. This cost will naturally be 0 if it is the first time drawing that {{C|Endless Agony}} in this way.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Endless Agony}} works well with any draw, most notably with {{C|Calculated Gamble}}, as {{C|Endless Agony}} increases the amount of cards in hand simply by being drawn, allowing you to play one copy without losing hand size. Similarly, {{R|Gambling Chip}} will allow you to draw more if an {{C|Endless Agony}} was in the original hand.\n\n* {{R|Wrist Blade}} increases the damage of both copies of this card by 4.\n\n* The created copy will be upgraded if the original copy was upgraded, or if {{C|Master Reality}} is active.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1936":{"pageid":1936,"ns":0,"title":"Feel No Pain","revisions":[{"revid":56761,"parentid":55776,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Feel No Pain\n|Image       = Red-FeelNoPain.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Whenever a card is {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}},<br>gain (3;4) {{KW|Block}}.\n|PowerGives = Block, Exhaust\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Feel No Pain\n|Image        = Icon FeelNoPain.png\n|Description  = Whenever you {{KW|Exhaust}} a card, gain X {{KW|Block}}.\n|Type         = Buff\n|Stacks       = Intensity\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n|InteractsWith = Exhaust\n|GivesToPlayer = Block\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Feel No Pain}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 3 (4 if upgraded) {{BD|Feel No Pain}}, which gives that amount of {{KW|Block}} whenever a card is {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* When playing a card that {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} a card, {{BD|Feel No Pain}} gives {{KW|Block}} ''after'' the played card is resolved. \n** Enemy {{BD|Thorns}} deals knockback damage ''before'' {{BD|Feel No Pain}} gives {{KW|Block}} when playing an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card that {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} something, such as {{C|Pummel}}, {{C|Sever Soul}} or {{C|Fiend Fire}}.\n** {{BD|Beat of Death}} deals damage ''before'' {{BD|Feel No Pain}} gives {{KW|Block}} when {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} another card because of a played card.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The {{KW|Block}} gained by {{BD|Feel No Pain}} is unaffected by {{BD|Frail}}, {{BD|Dexterity}} or {{BD|No Block}} from a previously played {{C|Panic Button}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 23: Testing Continues...'''\n** Feel No Pain+ card nerfed: Upgrade is now +1 rather than +2.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Feel No Pain card nerf. 4 -> 3 block. Upgraded: 6 -> 5 Block.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2449":{"pageid":2449,"ns":0,"title":"Impatience","revisions":[{"revid":50729,"parentid":36930,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Impatience\n|Image       = Colorless-Impatience.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = If you have no Attacks in your hand, draw (2;3) cards.\n|Keywords    = Draw, Hand\n}}\n{{C|Impatience}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. If you have no {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards in hand, it will draw 2 (3 if upgraded) cards.\n\n== Obtaining Impatience ==\n{{C|Impatience}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes well with hand-management through for example {{KW|Exhaust}} or [[Keywords#Discard|Discard]] effects.\n* When drawing it through {{R|Unceasing Top}}, the only card in hand will be {{C|Impatience}}, meaning it can be played.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As opposed to most cards and strategies in this game, this card pairs poorly with effects that allow you to draw cards, except for previously mentioned {{R|Unceasing Top}}. \n* It pairs poorly with {{R|Dead Branch}}, since {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards is a way to enable you to play {{C|Impatience}}, but this can possibly replace those cards with other {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 38: Bane'''\n** Adding colorless card Impatience.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1878":{"pageid":1878,"ns":0,"title":"Impervious","revisions":[{"revid":56416,"parentid":50463,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Impervious\n| Image       = Red-Impervious.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = Gain (30;40) {{KW|Block}}.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block, Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Impervious}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 30 (40 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}. {{C|Impervious}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2057":{"pageid":2057,"ns":0,"title":"Masterful Stab","revisions":[{"revid":56116,"parentid":55853,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Masterful Stab\n|Image       = Green-MasterfulStab.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Costs 1 additional {{Icon|GE}} for each time you lose HP this combat.<br>Deal (12;16) damage.\n|Keywords    = Energy\n}}\n{{C|Masterful Stab}} is a 0 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 12 (16 if upgraded) damage, and costs 1 more {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' for every time you lose HP this combat, no matter the source or amount of this HP loss.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* If {{C|Masterful Stab}} costs 0 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''', {{R|Wrist Blade}} will increase the damage of this card by 4.\n\n* If {{C|Masterful Stab}} costs 2 or more {{Icon|GE}} Energy, it will be able to trigger {{R|Necronomicon}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If this card is created during combat, such as through {{C|Metamorphosis}}, an {{P|Attack Potion}} or {{R|Dead Branch}}, it will start at 0 {{Icon|GE}}-cost. \n** This is unlike {{C|Blood for Blood}}, which takes HP that was lost before the card existed into account. \n\n* If it is stolen by [[Bronze Automaton]]'s {{BD|Minion|Minions}}, it will not change cost while it was in {{BD|Stasis}}. For example if it was stolen at 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost, and the player takes more damage, it will still be returned at 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost.\n\n* The '''Energy''' {{Icon|GE}}-cost randomization of {{BD|Confused}} or {{P|Snecko Oil}} will override the current {{Icon|GE}}-cost of {{C|Masterful Stab}}. Once randomized this way, the {{Icon|GE}}-cost will continue increasing as expected until it is randomized again.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act'''\n** Damage taken per turn checks for cards like Masterful Stab were not correctly resetting.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 49: The Designer'''\n** Fixed cards like Blood for Blood and Masterful Stab being affected outside of combat.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Effects that trigger on damage like Masterful Stab now interacts properly with damage prevention effects like Buffer.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 39: We Meet Again!'''\n** Masterful Stab card reworked.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** Masterful Stab card gets a minor damage buff.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2276":{"pageid":2276,"ns":0,"title":"Meditate","revisions":[{"revid":56622,"parentid":55856,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Meditate\n|Image       = Purple-Meditate.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Put (1 card;2 cards) from your discard pile into your hand and {{KW|Retain}} (it;them).<br>Enter {{KW|Calm}}.<br>End your turn.\n| GivesToPlayer = Calm, Retain, End Turn\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Retain}} {{Keyword Infobox|Calm}}\n{{C|Meditate}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It allows you to pick 1 card (2 cards if upgraded) from your discard pile to put into your hand and {{KW|Retain}}. Then it makes you enter the {{KW|Calm}} {{KW|Stance}} and ends your turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* When entering {{KW|Calm}} if you are not in {{KW|Calm}} yet, you will switch {{KW|Stance}}, which results in the following:\n** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand. \n*** However, as {{C|Meditate}} ends your turn, it will not be able to be played anymore.\n** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n\n* Being in {{KW|Calm}} has certain effects:\n** Playing {{C|Inner Peace}} will draw cards.\n** {{BD|Like Water}} from {{C|Like Water}} will give {{KW|Block}} at the end of your turn. As {{C|Meditate}} ends your turn, this will trigger immediately.\n\n* When you exit {{KW|Calm}}, it has the additional effect of giving you 2 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy'''. This increases to 3 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' if you have {{R|Violet Lotus}}.\n\n* With {{C|Establishment}}, every card {{KW|Retain|Retained}} this way will decrease in {{Icon|PE}}-cost.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Unlike other retain effects, {{C|Meditate}} is able to maintain {{KW|Ethereal}} cards.\n** For this, the {{KW|Ethereal}} card needs to end up in your discard pile, which can only happen through {{KW|Scry}} or [[Keywords#Discard|Discard]] effects.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Playing this card twice through an effect like {{C|Omniscience}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}} will result in that effect being wasted, as the first copy played already ends your turn, preventing the second play.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2021":{"pageid":2021,"ns":0,"title":"Prepared","revisions":[{"revid":55480,"parentid":50488,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Prepared\n|Image       = Green-Prepared.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Draw (1;2) (card;cards).<br>Discard (1;2) (card;cards).\n|Keywords    = Draw, Discard\n}}\n{{C|Prepared}} is a 0 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It draws 1 card (2 cards if upgraded) and makes you select 1 card (2 cards if upgraded) in hand to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]].\n\n== Interactions == \n=== Order ===\n* Selecting which card(s) to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] happens ''after'' drawing, meaning that you can also choose the newly drawn card(s) to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]]. This also means that if you play {{C|Prepared}} without any other cards in hand, it will draw 1 card (2 cards if upgraded) and then immediately [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] the same card(s).\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Prepared}}'s [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] effect synergises with several [[Silent]] cards and relics: \n\n==== Cards ====\n* [[Keywords#Discard|Discarding]] {{C|Tactician}} or {{C|Reflex}} will immediately activate their effects.\n* {{C|Eviscerate}} is discounted by X {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' this turn, where X is the number of cards [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n* {{C|Sneaky Strike}} will now refund 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if also played this turn.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Tough Bandages}} will grant 3 {{KW|Block}} per card [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n* {{R|Tingsha}} will deal 3 damage to a random enemy per card [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n* {{R|Hovering Kite}} will generate 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if this is the first time a card has been [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] this turn.\n\n=== Neutral === \n* {{C|Prepared}} can also be used to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] cards with end-of-turn effects, like {{C|Burn}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} such as {{C|Regret}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The card art shows the same bag from {{R|Bag of Preparation}}.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1833":{"pageid":1833,"ns":0,"title":"Reaper","revisions":[{"revid":56385,"parentid":55915,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":" {{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Reaper\n| Image       = Red-Reaper.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = Deal (4;5) damage to ALL enemies. Heal HP equal to unblocked damage.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Heal, Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Reaper}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 4 (5 if upgraded) damage to '''ALL''' enemies and heals you for the amount of unblocked damage it dealt. You will only heal for the amount of HP actually lost by the enemy, so killing an enemy with damage remaining will only heal you for the HP they had left. {{C|Reaper}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* The healing from {{C|Reaper}} takes effect ''after'' receiving damage from {{BD|Thorns}} or {{BD|Sharp Hide}}, but before taking damage from {{BD|Beat of Death}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Magic Flower}} increases the effectiveness of any healing from {{C|Reaper}}.\n* Any increase to the damage output of {{C|Reaper}} will also boost its healing:\n** {{BD|Vulnerable}} on any of the enemies, particularly with {{R|Paper Phrog}}.\n** Any positive amount of {{BD|Strength}}. \n** {{BD|Vigor}}.\n** {{R|The Boot}} boosting its unblocked damage to 5.\n** Being in the {{KW|Wrath}} or {{KW|Divinity}} {{KW|Stance}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Healing cards cannot be generated mid-combat to avoid infinite healing, so {{C|Reaper}} cannot be created by {{C|Infernal Blade}}, {{C|Metamorphosis}} or {{R|Dead Branch}}. \n** However, if you already have a {{C|Reaper}} cards can be generated that allow you to heal to full HP regardless:\n*** Sources of {{BD|Strength}}, like {{C|Spot Weakness}} or {{C|Demon Form}}.\n*** Ways to increase the amount of {{C|Reaper|Reapers}} played, like {{C|Dual Wield}} or {{C|Exhume}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reaper}} suffers doubly from any penalty to its damage, meaning {{BD|Weak}} and negative {{BD|Strength}} are particularly harmful for this card.\n* {{C|Reaper}} relies on damaging enemies at the right moment, meaning that damage that you have no control over, such as from {{C|Combust}}, {{BD|Thorns}} or {{R|Stone Calendar}} can possibly reduce the healing you get from this card.\n\n== Bugs ==\n* '''Reaper''' can sometimes fail to heal under certain circumstances. \n* After lethal damage is dealt, combat will be ended after 1 second when updateDeathAnimation concludes that enemies are done dying. '''Reaper's''' heal action is added to the bottom of the queue and a WaitAction is added to the top. If additional actions take long enough, '''Reaper's''' heal will never be reached before combat is ended.\n** This is most noticeable combats with multiple enemies, like {{M|Reptomancer}}, with delays like {{R|Charon's Ashes}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The {{M|Jaw Worm}} and {{M|Red Louse}} are depicted in the card art.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Improved lifesteal logic for Reaper and Shelled Parasite.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 55: Blur'''\n** Reaper card now heals the correct amount if the player has The Boot relic.\n** Adding VFX for Reaper card.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!'''\n** Reaper now heals as part of the attack now, not after (you heal before thorns hit you).\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1859":{"pageid":1859,"ns":0,"title":"Rupture","revisions":[{"revid":56618,"parentid":56615,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Rupture\n| Image       = Red-Rupture.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Whenever you lose HP from a card,<br>gain (1;2) {{BD|Strength}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Rupture\n| PowerGives = Strength, Lose HP\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Rupture\n| Image        = Icon Rupture.png\n| Description  = Whenever you lose HP from a card, gain X {{BD|Strength}}.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n| GivesToPlayer = Strength\n| InteractsWith = Lose HP\n}}\n{{C|Rupture}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Rupture}}, which gives that amount of {{BD|Strength}} whenever a card causes you to lose HP.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{C|Hemokinesis}} will not benefit from the {{BD|Strength}} gained as a result of {{BD|Rupture}} until played again, as {{BD|Rupture}} triggers ''after'' the card is already resolved.\n\n* HP loss caused by {{C|Pain}} applies ''after'' the effects of the card that triggered it, meaning {{BD|Rupture}} will trigger ''after'' the card that triggered {{C|Pain}} has already dealt damage.\n** However, if you have {{C|Pain}} in hand and use a different card to cause an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} to be played, such as through {{C|Havoc}}, the first card will trigger {{C|Pain}} and therefore {{BD|Rupture}} ''before'' the {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} takes effect.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Playing any {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} with {{R|Blue Candle}} triggers {{BD|Rupture}}.\n\n* {{C|Reaper}} gives healing based on damage dealt, and therefore increases with {{BD|Strength}}. This can be used to regain HP lost as a result of triggering this card.\n\n* Any card that can cause you to lose HP can trigger {{BD|Rupture}}:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Bloodletting}}, {{C|Hemokinesis}} and {{C|J.A.X.}} can repeatedly be played to trigger it.\n* {{C|Offering}} can be played to trigger it and then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}.\n* {{C|Combust}} and {{C|Brutality}} will trigger it every turn.\n* {{C|Regret}} will trigger it if it is in your hand at the end of your turn.\n* {{C|Pain}} makes every other card in hand cost 1 HP, allowing you to rack up large quantities of {{BD|Strength}} quickly.\n* {{C|Burn}} and {{C|Decay}} deal damage instead of causing HP loss directly. This will still trigger {{BD|Rupture}}, as long as the damage is not fully negated by {{KW|Block}}, and therefore causes you to lose HP.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The amount of {{BD|Strength}} gained from triggering {{BD|Rupture}} does not scale with the amount of HP lost.\n\n* Losing HP when playing a card, as a result of {{BD|Thorns}}, {{BD|Sharp Hide}} or {{BD|Beat of Death}}, will not trigger {{BD|Rupture}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Technically {{C|Blasphemy}} deals 99999 damage instead of killing the player directly. In theory this could be used to activate {{C|Rupture}}, although unpractical in reality.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Rupture+ card buffed. Strength gain increased from 1 -> 2.\n** Rupture+ card nerfed. Energy cost 0 -> 1.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating icon for Rupture power.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2450":{"pageid":2450,"ns":0,"title":"Smite","revisions":[{"revid":50765,"parentid":37726,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Smite\n|Image       = Colorless-Smite.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Special\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = {{KW|Retain}}. <br>Deal (12;16) damage. <br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Retain}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Smite}} is a 1 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 12 (16 if upgraded) damage and then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}. It has {{KW|Retain}}, meaning it will not be discarded when you end your turn.\n\n== Creating Smite ==\n{{C|Smite}} can only be created in combat, by playing {{C|Battle Hymn}} or {{C|Carve Reality}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Starting when you have {{C|Master Reality}} in play, {{C|Battle Hymn}} and {{C|Carve Reality}} will create upgraded {{C|Smite|Smites}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2477":{"pageid":2477,"ns":0,"title":"Transmutation","revisions":[{"revid":55517,"parentid":51094,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Transmutation\n|Image       = Colorless-Transmutation.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = -1\n|Description = Add X random(; {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}}) Colorless cards into your hand. They cost 0 this turn.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Transmutation}} is an X {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It adds X {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards into your hand, which cost 0 this turn. If this {{C|Transmutation}} is upgraded, it will add upgraded {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards instead. It then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} itself.\n\n== Obtaining Transmutation ==\n{{C|Transmutation}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Chemical X}} makes {{C|Transmutation}} apply 2 more times, regardless of the amount of {{Icon|CE}} '''Energy''' used to play it.\n* If played using {{P|Distilled Chaos}}, {{C|Havoc}}, or {{C|Omniscience}}, it will play for the full current {{Icon|CE}} '''Energy''' without actually using any.\n* Can be used with 0 {{Icon|CE}} '''Energy''' to advance {{R|Ink Bottle}} or {{R|Letter Opener}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If a card generated by this card exceeds your hand size limit, it gets added to the discard pile.\n* If {{C|Transmutation}} is duplicated with an effect such as a {{P|Duplication Potion}} or {{C|Burst}}, the value of '''X''' will also be used for the copy.\n* Being an X-cost, {{C|Transmutation}} can be {{C|Recycle|Recycled}} to double the current {{Icon|CE}} '''Energy'''.\n* It will not count as a 0-cost card for {{C|Scrape}} or {{C|All for One}}.\n\n* Some {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards cannot be generated, as they have some permanent effect out of combat, or can only be obtained from another source.\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Bandage Up}}\n* {{C|Apparition}}\n* {{C|Bite}}\n* {{C|J.A.X.}}\n* {{C|Ritual Dagger}} \n* {{C|Shiv}}\n* {{C|Beta}}\n* {{C|Insight}}\n* {{C|Miracle}}\n* {{C|Omega}}\n* {{C|Safety}}\n* {{C|Smite}}\n* {{C|Through Violence}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Before Weekly Patch 8, {{C|Transmutation}} was a 0-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} with the following text: {{KW|Transform}} your Hand. {{KW|Exhaust}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Corruption and other cost reducing cards no longer make X cost cards like Transmutation and Malaise display cost 0.\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 37: Darkness'''\n** Transmutation card buffed. Cards acquired by Transmutation now cost 0 for the turn.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 12: Lunar New Year'''\n** Transmutation+ no longer gives you a free card.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Shiv and J.A.X can no longer spawn from effects like Jack Of All Trades and Transmutation.\n** Removing 'Spend all [R].' from all X-cost cards for consistency.\n** Fixed bug where cost X cards do not work with energy gain cards if played too fast.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Transmutation reworked. Cost X -> Gain X random colorless cards (+upgrades)\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 7: Setting Up All the Things'''\n** Fixed typo in Transmutation card description.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2303":{"pageid":2303,"ns":0,"title":"Worship","revisions":[{"revid":56003,"parentid":54824,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Worship\n|Image       = Purple-Worship.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = (;{{KW|Retain}}.<br>)Gain 5 {{BD|Mantra}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Mantra}}{{C|Worship}} is a 2 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 5 {{BD|Mantra}} and 4 {{KW|Block}}. When reaching 10 {{BD|Mantra}}, all of it will be removed and you will enter the {{KW|Divinity}} {{KW|Stance}}. When upgraded, it gets {{KW|Retain}}, meaning it will not be discarded when you end your turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Brilliance}} increases in damage whenever you gain {{BD|Mantra}}.\n\n* All {{BD|Mantra}} sources synergize with eachother: {{C|Prostrate}}, {{C|Pray}}, {{C|Devotion}} and {{R|Damaru}} work well with {{C|Worship}}.\n\n* When entering {{KW|Divinity}} if you are not in {{KW|Divinity}} yet, you will gain 3 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' and switch {{KW|Stance}}, which results in the following:\n** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n\n* While in {{KW|Divinity}}, all damage from {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} is tripled. This does not affect damage from effects such as {{BD|Panache}} or {{BD|Thorns}}, or relics such as {{R|Mercury Hourglass}}.\n\n* As the upgraded version of {{C|Worship}} {{KW|Retain|Retains}}, {{C|Establishment}} will decrease it in {{Icon|PE}}-cost at the end of a turn, unless it already costs 0.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}